Recommended Start Order
Phase 1

Build:

apps/web
apps/admin
packages/ui
packages/types
packages/database
Phase 2

Add:

packages/utils
packages/config
docs
scripts
Phase 3

Add:

apps/api
mobile app
workers

---------------------------------------------------------------------------

apps/

Contains runnable applications.

apps/web

Customer-facing ecommerce website.

Responsibilities
Homepage
Product listing
Product detail pages
Search / filters
Cart
Checkout
User login/signup
Order history
Order tracking
Suggested Structure
apps/web/
│── app/
│── components/
│── lib/
│── hooks/
│── public/
│── styles/
apps/admin

Business operating dashboard.

Responsibilities
Dashboard overview
Product CRUD
Category CRUD
Order management
Expense tracking
Inventory management
Analytics
Customer records
Settings
Suggested Structure
apps/admin/
│── app/
│── components/
│── lib/
│── hooks/
│── styles/
apps/api (optional future)

Backend service (NestJS later if needed).

Use Cases
Complex business logic
Webhooks
Third-party integrations
Mobile API
Background jobs
packages/

Reusable shared code.

packages/ui

Shared UI components used by both web and admin.

Examples:

Button
Input
Modal
Card
Table
Sidebar
Navbar
ProductCard

Why?

Build once, use everywhere.

packages/types

Shared TypeScript types.

Examples:

Product
Order
User
Expense
Category
InventoryMovement

Why?

Keeps frontend/admin consistent.

packages/utils

Reusable helper functions.

Examples:

formatCurrency()
formatDate()
generateSlug()
calculateProfit()
calculateDiscount()
packages/database

Database-related logic.

Contains:

Supabase client
Query helpers
DB utilities
Validation helpers
Shared data access logic
packages/config

Shared configuration files.

Contains:

tsconfig
eslint config
prettier config

Why?

All apps follow same coding standards.

docs/

Project documentation.

Examples:

database-schema.md
api-plan.md
feature-roadmap.md
deployment-guide.md
scripts/

Automation scripts.

Examples:

seed.ts
backup.ts
generate-types.ts
cleanup.ts